        "question": "Based on the chest X-ray findings, what is the most likely location and characteristic of the lesion in the right hemithorax, and what is its relationship to the surrounding structures? \n\nA) The lesion is located in the middle zone of the right hemithorax and appears as a solid mass, closely associated with the posterior ribs.\nB) The lesion is located in the lower zone of the right hemithorax, appears cystic, and is primarily associated with the anterior ribs.\nC) The lesion is located in the middle and lower zones of the right hemithorax, appears as a large cystic mass with septations, and is associated with the posterior ribs.\nD) The lesion is located in the upper zone of the right hemithorax, appears solid, and is associated with the mediastinum.\nE) The lesion is located diffusely throughout the right hemithorax, has both solid and cystic components, and is not associated with any specific rib structure.\nF) The lesion is located in the middle zone of the right hemithorax, appears as a cystic mass without septations, and is associated with the anterior ribs.",
